d back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both marked unhealthy in release history; v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. Actions taken: (1) rollback to v2.3.0 initially returned a partial_failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1. (2) Retried rollback to v2.3.0, which completed across us-east, us-west and eu-west. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure cause and the orchestrator partial failure; confirm v2.3.1 fix before any re-release."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01N22eg18RjMYRGE3FDYtJJQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002).\n\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt to roll back to v2.3.0 failed partway through with an orchestrator error. us-east had moved to v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I retried once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both marked unhealthy, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** SEV2 incident **INC-0001** is open for checkout-api. The first request to open it timed out, but the incident had been created, so I didn't open a duplicate. Its summary covers the partial failure, the retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-up: someone should find out why v2.3.1 failed and why the first rollback only partially applied before v2.3.1 is re-released.", "type": "text"}]}]}